{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/67","id":4975246696,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSLn-hc8AAAABKIw9aA","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/67","diff_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/67.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/67.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/67","number":67,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Allow explicit retry after a failed connection close","user":{"login":"codexcoder21","id":216437543,"node_id":"U_kgDODOaTJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216437543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21","html_url":"https://github.com/codexcoder21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The owner asked on 2026-10-21: \"Then, do another round, Your goal is to add end-to-end integration tests which identify bugs (the tests should initially fail), and then fix the bug in the implementation.\" Moving UrlProtocol to [jvm-libp2p snapshot-38](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/846) left five UrlProtocol tests failing because callers could not retry a physical connection close after a failed first attempt, as described in https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/61.\n\n`Connection.retryClose()` explicitly requests another attempt after a settled failure. `ConnectionOverNetty.close()` keeps its original shared result. Explicit callers share the latest pending attempt; a successful attempt stays terminal, and each caller receives a derived future that cannot change the privately owned operation. Existing stream-backed relay connections inherit delegation to their stream close operation. README and API KDoc describe these contracts.\n\nTwelve real-connection scenarios now cover TCP/Noise/Yamux and three-host relay operation, 8,192 concurrent retry observations, 1,000 consecutive injected close failures, callback and handler re-entry, transport-owned failures, peer closure, success boundaries, and caller future changes. The additional [REV67 scenario](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/REV67-review-20261023/lane-evidence) holds retry attempt 2 while the peer closes the physical socket and `channelInactive` re-enters both close APIs. It verifies that all three retry observers receive attempt 2's own failure exactly once, ordinary close retains failure 1, and a later retry succeeds without physical request 3. The reviewer's assertions are unchanged; the only port adjustment is repository formatting.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Before the implementation fix, nine recovery tests failed at runtime on their first attempt against the old helper; initial-success and relay default controls passed as expected. [Original failure proof and implementation review](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/JL61-evidence-20261022/lane-evidence).\n- Added peer-close/pending-retry scenario: 3/3 first-attempt passes on the PR implementation, and 3/3 first-attempt assertion failures against the [reviewer's closed-channel shortcut mutation](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/FIX67-shortcut-mutation-20261023). The mutation incorrectly reports success for a still-pending retry. Full failure stacks are preserved.\n- Final head `43eab3dc7f2a03e8144b9fa99cf3811cb0fbda4d`: three fresh targeted/neighbour runs each passed 24/24 on the first attempt, with zero failures, errors, or skips. This includes the original 23 cases and the added scenario. Gradle durations were 15/13/13 seconds. `:libp2p:assemble`, `:libp2p:spotlessCheck`, and `:libp2p:detekt` passed each sweep.\n- One full repository suite under `/tmp/claude-501/complete-suite.lock`: **1,226 tests; 1,203 passed; 21 failed; 2 pre-existing disabled tests**. All 12 retry scenarios passed first attempt. The failed set contains all 20 known failures from unchanged `develop` at `e15e0f1947842be7ef6836c116c14ba47cc8eea1`, plus one additional Noise harness failure; the expected exact-20 result was therefore refuted. The 20 known failures are native TLS/QUIC initialization, subsequent fixed-port bind failures after failed host setup, and the Kubo test expecting an external localhost service. The additional case, `NoiseHandshakeOffEventLoopTest.remote read timeout fails saturated handshakes while responder crypto is queued`, reported 120 queued responder tasks versus 118 failed dials. Its cause remains unconfirmed. The Noise implementation and harness bytecode match develop; two fresh Gradle controls and 30 direct-harness controls on unchanged develop passed. Twenty first-attempt concurrent controls on the PR head also passed. These later controls do not erase the failed full-suite result or establish a fix, and no Noise implementation/test change was guessed. No tests were disabled, weakened, or given larger timeouts.\n- Separate test-comprehensiveness and implementation review passes found no remaining issue in this retry change. [REV67 review](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/REV67-review-20261023/lane-evidence) also confirmed JVM default-method compatibility with the existing compiled relay implementation. The new pending-retry case addresses its one SHOULD-FIX finding.\n\nThe GitHub Actions build workflow fails to start for every inspected commit, including unchanged `develop`: its suites report `startup_failure` with zero jobs/check runs. Repository Actions permissions remain `allowed_actions=local_only`, while the inherited workflow uses external Actions including `actions/checkout`; this mismatch is sufficient to block startup, though no run annotation excludes additional causes. The expected `gradle (ubuntu-latest)` and `gradle (windows-latest)` jobs have not run or been verified green. Informational Kotlin checks are reported separately; they do not establish an Actions pass. No workflow policy, CI rerun, enqueue, merge, artifact publication, deployment or service restart was performed.\n\n[FIX67 findings, three-run controls, full XML/stacks, exact baseline comparison, memory samples and review](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/FIX67-evidence-20261023/lane-evidence).\n\n[Remaining repository verification work](https://www.handoff.wasmserver.com/handoffs/hf-2026-10-22-restore-required-verification-for-jvm-libp2p-explicit-close-retry).\n\nFixes https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/61\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-22T22:57:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T01:56:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5cdf88fa603943fd53a350c77db0aa041d4ac8da","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/67/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/67/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCode